reasoning:
Confirmed: the recorded status diverges from the actual wire status when WriteHeader is called after the header was already written (either via WriteHeaderNow, Write, WriteString, or Flush). The fix: return early in WriteHeader when already written.

This matches upstream gin master:
```go
func (w *responseWriter) WriteHeader(code int) {
	if code > 0 && w.status != code {
		if w.Written() {
			debugPrint("[WARNING] Headers were already written. Wanted to override status code %d with %d", w.status, code)
			return
		}
		w.status = code
	}
}
```

